---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Where to Apply" description="Privacy information for visitors to Where to Apply.">
  <main class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <a class="link text-sm" href="/">← Where to Apply</a>
    <h1 class="mt-8 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-fg-2 leading-relaxed">
      <p>Where to Apply is a public directory. You can browse its pages without creating an account, submitting a resume, or entering personal information. Search filters and the application checklist run in your browser. Checklist state is stored locally in that browser so it can be used on a later visit; it is not submitted as an account or application to this site.</p>
      <p>The site uses Vercel Web Analytics and PostHog for anonymous or pseudonymous usage measurement, as configured for the deployment. These services may process technical request information and interaction events to report site usage. The project does not use the checklist to build a job seeker profile and does not sell visitor information. For details about processing by those providers, consult their own privacy documentation.</p>
      <p>When you follow a link to a job board, company, community, social network, or another website, that destination operates under its own privacy policy and terms. Where to Apply does not control what those sites collect or how they process applications. Review the destination's policies before sharing personal information or applying for a role.</p>
      <p>Privacy questions or requests about this website can be raised through the <a class="link" href="https://github.com/khardikk/where-to-apply/issues">project issue tracker</a> or by contacting the maintainer through <a class="link" href="https://hardikk.dev">Hardikk's website</a>. This page describes the site's current features and may be updated when the deployment or analytics configuration changes. Last reviewed: October 17, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
